---
/*
 * ============================================================================
 * FILE: src/pages/check-inbox.astro
 * ROUTE: /check-inbox  (static HTML page, prerendered at build time)
 * ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
 * WHAT THIS IS
 *   A dead-simple "interstitial" / confirmation-instruction page. After a
 *   visitor submits the newsletter subscribe form (double opt-in flow), the
 *   subscribe handler redirects the browser here. The page's ONLY job is to
 *   tell the human: "we sent you an email — go click the link in it."
 *
 * SINGLE RESPONSIBILITY
 *   Display static reassurance/instruction copy. Nothing more. It performs NO
 *   logic: no data fetching, no token reading, no form handling, no auth, no
 *   database calls, no JavaScript. It is a pure presentational leaf page.
 *
 * HOW IT FITS THE ARCHITECTURE
 *   The subscribe flow is a classic double opt-in:
 *     1. User submits email (protected by Turnstile bot check + honeypot).
 *     2. A Pages Function inserts a pending subscriber into Supabase and asks
 *        Resend to send a confirmation email containing a one-time token link.
 *     3. The browser is redirected to THIS page → "check your inbox".
 *     4. User clicks the link in the email → a separate confirm endpoint
 *        verifies the token and flips the subscriber to confirmed.
 *   This file is step 3's landing page only. All the security-sensitive work
 *   (token generation/verification, entitlement gating, signature checks,
 *   honeypot, Turnstile, RLS enforcement) lives in the Pages Functions and
 *   Supabase — deliberately NOT here.
 *
 * DEPENDENCIES (imports)
 *   - BaseLayout.astro: the shared site shell (<html>, <head> meta/OG tags,
 *     nav, footer, global styles). This page injects only its <h1>/<p> body
 *     into that layout's default slot. `title`/`description` feed the shell's
 *     <title> and meta description / OG tags.
 *
 * WHO DEPENDS ON THIS
 *   - The newsletter subscribe handler (Pages Function / client redirect)
 *     sends users here by URL. If you rename or move this route, update that
 *     redirect target or subscribers will land on a 404 mid-signup.
 *   - No other page imports this component; it is a route endpoint, not a
 *     reusable component.
 *
 * SECURITY / GOTCHA NOTES
 *   - This page is intentionally trust-free: it reads NO query params, tokens,
 *     or user input, so there is no injection, token-leak, or entitlement
 *     surface here. Keep it that way — do not add token handling or reflect
 *     any URL parameter into the DOM, or you introduce a leak/XSS vector where
 *     none exists today.
 *   - It is safe to serve to anyone (unauthenticated, pre-confirmation). It
 *     reveals nothing sensitive; the copy is generic and identical for all
 *     visitors, which avoids confirming whether a given email exists.
 *   - Being fully static, it is prerendered and cacheable at the CDN edge with
 *     no per-request cost or backend dependency.
 * ============================================================================
 */
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import site from '../data/site.json';
const c = (site as any).checkInbox || {};
---

{/*
  Presentational body only. All markup below is slotted into BaseLayout's
  default slot. Do NOT use HTML <!-- --> comments in this template — they ship
  to the browser; only these {/* JSX comments are stripped at build.
*/}
<BaseLayout title={c.seo?.title || 'Almost there — areyoustillreading'} description={c.seo?.description || 'Confirm your subscription.'}>
  <h1 data-cms="checkInbox.heading">{c.heading || 'Almost there'}</h1>
  {/* Instruction copy for the double opt-in: prompt the user to click the
      confirmation link we emailed. The spam-folder nudge is a deliverability
      fail-safe — confirmation mail (via Resend) is a common false-positive for
      spam filters, and a missed link silently strands the signup. */}
  <p data-cms="checkInbox.body">{c.body || "Check your inbox for a confirmation link to finish subscribing. If it's not there in a minute, check your spam folder."}</p>
  {/* Escape hatch back to the homepage so a user who is done (or gave up)
      isn't dead-ended on this static page. */}
  <p><a href="/" data-cms="checkInbox.home">{c.home || '← Home'}</a></p>
</BaseLayout>
